      },
      "message": "fix(post): refuse Fanuc G76 when the start point is above material\n\nCarry `start_in_air` on `cl::ThreadCycle`, serialize it as optional\n`AIR 1` on `THREAD` records (absent reads false), and expose it to post\nscripts as `StartInAir`.\n\nCompute `start_in_air` across the full rapid-infeed axial band against\nthe revolved part, stock and prior turning, grooving, facing and\ndrilling operations. Refuse G76 by name in `assets/posts/fanuc-lathe.cps`\nwhen `StartInAir !== true` so the control never moves the insert into\nmaterial at rapid traverse.\n\nAllow `turning::thread` to start a pass in free air in front of a free\nend face and stop `revolve::lattice` from re-adding out-of-domain window\nendpoints after `retain`.\n\nFixes #2878",
